      "rationale": "This simplification adds a guarded fact about the imported applyBin symbol rather than defining a new proof term. Stage 1 separately proves only a Float-typed applyBin-to-subF claim, not this exact Val-typed, isFloat-guarded, asFloat-bearing rule, so the canonical rule does not qualify as PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-fc66c723d628ad8e811c12c35a08f3b4345486c0dfef2593966c9dbe4c211ecf",
      "start_line": 21,
      "text": "  rule applyBin(\"-\", A:Val, B:Val) => subF(asFloat(A), asFloat(B))\n    requires isFloat(A) andBool isFloat(B)\n    [simplification]"
    }
